From a45b6eb43bf6dc1f63e665095c78ca239858bad6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 20:56:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-oneplus-hotdog: give the Bluetooth
 UART an alias

The Bluetooth controller never initialised on this board, and the reason
is one line earlier than anyone looked: the UART it hangs off never
probed.

qcom_geni_serial_probe() takes its line number from an alias, trying
"serial" and then "hsuart". With neither present of_alias_get_id()
returns -ENODEV and the probe stops:

  qcom_geni_serial c8c000.serial: Invalid line -19

So there is no ttyHS, no serdev child under serial@c8c000, and no
controller for hci_uart to bind. hci0 was reported down with a locally
administered address and no firmware download, which is exactly what a
controller that was never created looks like from userspace.

sm8150-google-flame, sm8150-xiaomi-nabu and sm8150-xiaomi-raphael all
declare hsuart0 = &uart13 for the same UART. Do the same here.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
index dadf512a04c29..750dc631e1089 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@ memory@80000000 {
 
 	aliases {
 		display0 = &framebuffer0;
+		hsuart0 = &uart13;
 	};
 
 	chosen {
